#### Task 2 – Cloud Computing Overview
I learned how computing evolved from physical servers to modern cloud platforms.

I learned that early systems relied heavily on physical servers, which were expensive, difficult to scale, and often underused.

Virtualisation improved this by allowing multiple virtual machines to run on the same physical hardware.

Cloud computing developed further by allowing organisations to rent computing resources over the internet instead of purchasing and managing all hardware themselves.

